    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it felt different though. an adrenaline rush is usually pretty random, but this was rhythmic. like, if the candle was a massive red wick, i felt this sharp, heavy thud in my chest at that exact millisecond. it was like my nervous system was receiving the data packet before the UI even rendered it. i've been tracking my BPM alongside the 1m charts and the correlation is actually getting weirdly high. how can you say it's just stress when the timing is literally frame-perfect?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
